        "why": "The pipelined family offers 1 result/cycle throughput, which is necessary to meet the 32 MSPS constraint. We narrow the ranges to the region where accuracy was previously met (data_width 16-18, n_iter 14-16) to ensure the max_abs_err constraint is satisfied while maximizing Fmax."
      }
    ],
    "rationale": "We need to add the `pipelined` family because the current best throughput (10.5 MSPS) is insufficient. The `pipelined` family's 1 result/cycle throughput is the only way to reach 32 MSPS. We focus on the parameter ranges that previously met the accuracy constraint to ensure we find a feasible design."
  }
